# The responsive sudo prompt (task 014 P3d), over the native Settings page: the shared Dialog "Sudo Password" with a
# masked Password field, the status line and Cancel / OK. sudoprompt drives cp0_sudo_prompt_ui directly (the harness
# links no sudo coordinator): open = SHOW_PROMPT, busy = START_WORKER, wrong = SHOW_AUTH_ERROR, close = DESTROY_PROMPT.
# First with the on-screen keyboard forced (typed password masked, Authenticating..., wrong password, Cancel by a tap
# on the dialog's button), then with a physical keyboard (no keyboard, buttons visible; Enter / Esc). Review only.
title sudo prompt
review
env APPLAUNCH_SETTINGS_UI native
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
env APPLAUNCH_OSK force
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
launch Settings
sudoprompt open
shot sudo_osk
type secret
shot sudo_osk_typed
key ENTER
shot sudo_osk_busy
sudoprompt wrong
shot sudo_osk_wrong
key ESC
wait 300
shot sudo_osk_closed
